      "The brain science here is interesting: intrinsically motivated service (done because it's right) activates deeper, more sustained reward circuitry than extrinsically motivated service (done for recognition). You feel better — genuinely, sustainably — when you give with no expectation of return. The reward is in the giving itself.",
      'The Anointed One taught: "When you give to the needy, do not let your left hand know what your right hand is doing, so that your giving may be in secret." Not because secrecy is the point, but because the discipline of not seeking recognition trains your motivation toward something purer. The ultimate freedom is doing the right thing with no audience.',
