      'Recovery ego is subtle. It sounds like this: "I don\'t think I can be around people who aren\'t doing the work." "They just don\'t understand what real recovery looks like." "I\'ve been through things that most people haven\'t." All of this may be true. And all of it can become a way of staying separate, staying above, avoiding the genuine humility that recovery requires at every stage.',
      "The Anointed One said the greatest among you will be the servant of all. Not the most enlightened. Not the most spiritually advanced. The servant of all. The willingness to descend, to enter the mess, to be with the struggling person without any trace of superiority — that's the apex of recovery. That's Empower.",
