      "Your integrity is protected when your thoughts, your words, and your actions are aligned. When you don't lie to preserve comfort. When you do what you say you'll do. When you tell the truth even when it's inconvenient. Integrity is not a moral luxury — it's the foundation on which every relationship, every commitment, and every recovery practice stands. Without integrity, nothing else holds.",
