      "Mentors and sponsors are people who have walked ahead of you on the path and are willing to walk with you. Not to do the work for you, but to guide you when you're lost, to hold you when you're struggling, and to see possibilities in you that you cannot yet see yourself. A good mentor is honest, available, and has done their own work. Choose wisely. Use consistently.",
      "Recovery principles are the accumulated wisdom of countless people who have walked this road before you — distilled into principles, slogans, steps, and practices. They don't replace your own discernment, but they provide a tested framework that your addicted brain cannot generate on its own. When in doubt, return to the principles. They have been refined through more experience than you have.",
      'Community is the group of people who share your commitment to recovery — who see you, who will call you out, who will celebrate with you, who will sit with you in the hard times. This is not optional support. It is structural support. The research on recovery consistently shows that social connection is among the most protective factors for long-term recovery. Isolation kills. Community heals.',
